	(gr_text "OPENAIO 8L HDI 1+6+1 (2026-10-15)  1.0 mm (0.997 with mask), 1 oz on all layers, ENIG\nStackup = OpenAIO-Whoop (NextPCB-confirmed, D123): 1080 / 1080 / core / 2116 / core / 1080 / 1080\nL1  F.Cu  parts (FC on top), high-side FET +BATT pours, phase pours\nL2  In1   GND plane (microvia target), /CSA+ corridor at the battery pad\nL3  In2   signals (Base), GND fill\nL4  In3   +BATT pour over the high-side FETs, +10V; Core links\nL5  In4   rails: +3V3, +3.3V, +4v5, +5V_USB, +10V; Core signals\nL6  In5   signals (Core) + +5V pour\nL7  In6   GND plane (microvia target)\nL8  B.Cu  parts (ESC side), low-side FET GND pours, phase pours\n\nVIAS (layer pairs: Micro L1-L2, Buried L2-L7, Micro L7-L8)\nthrough 0.35/0.20 (power 0.5/0.3) only where F.Cu and B.Cu copper both connect\nmicro   0.25/0.10  L1-L2, L7-L8 (in pad, filled + capped); stagger 0.25 mm from the buried via = HDI rank 1\nburied  0.33/0.15  L2-L7 (0.74 mm span, 5:1); a microvia stacked on it prices as rank 2 (+0.34 USD/board @1000)\nKeys (macOS): V through, Cmd+V microvia, Option+Shift+V buried (active pair)\nAfter routing: tools/via_types.py --buried-size 0.33/0.15, tools/via_nudge.py, tools/power_paths.py"
